                <pb facs="0689" n="629" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg629"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The following are the officers who now hold appointments on the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nymphe:</hi> Commander, George Huntingford; lieutenants,
                    Patrick M. Stewart, Ernest L. C. Muntz, Charles J. Wintour; paymaster, Charles
                    E. C. Webb; chief engineer, Robert S. G. Borgate; surgeon, Henry E. South;
                    assistant engineer, Thomas O. Jameson; boatswain, Richard J. Chappell.</p>
                <p>The following hold appointments on the <hi rendition="#italic">Pheasant:</hi>
                    Lieutenant-commander, Frank A. Garforth; second lieutenants, Henry R. Shipster,
                    Arthur B. Hughes; surgeon, Edgar F. Mortimer; engineer, Albert E. Collins;
                    assistant paymaster in charge, Henry Constantine; gunner, Frederick S.
                    Farlow.</p>
            </div>
